From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe-rule: build against Linux 6.12 / OpenWrt 25.12

Three unrelated errors surface when qca-nss-ppe-rule is built with the
25.12 toolchain:

1. Linux 6.8 changed struct ctl_table's proc_handler to take a const
   pointer.  ppe_rfs_mcast_rfs_enable_handler() still takes a mutable
   one, which 6.12 rejects with -Wincompatible-pointer-types.  Same
   change as 0021 for ppe_vp.

2. OpenWrt 25.12 enables -Wmissing-prototypes and builds with -Werror.
   The vendor sources define many helpers at file scope with no
   prototype in any header and call them only from the same file.  They
   are given internal linkage (static), the same way the rest of the
   module is written.  No symbol touched here is referenced from another
   translation unit or exported: each name occurs in exactly one .c file
   of the package and in none of its headers.

3. strlcpy() has been removed from the kernel; strscpy() replaces it.
   Both stop at a NUL-terminated source and truncate to the destination
   size, so the dev-name copy behaves as before.

No behaviour change: the handler keeps its body, the helpers keep their
bodies, and the copy still truncates to fit.
